"","","r","Completed in the early 1990s, this beautiful mosque is worth taking a look at."],["Cairo Puppet Theatre","activity",30.05304,31.24645,"Azbakia Park","","","","","r","A fantastic way to spend an afternoon with the kids. The Cairo Puppet Theatre puts on a variety of shows including myths, fairy tales and fun children's stories."],["Karam El Sham","restaurant",30.05053,31.24065,"","","","","","r","There are big crowds and queues outside but for good reason. The staff makes a real effort to speak English to help you order and receive vour food after waiting. Both the sharwama and the rice are tasty."],["Akram Gad Restaurant","restaurant",30.05273,31.24296,"13, 26th of July St.","","","","","r","Fast food restaurant, done Egyptian style. Usually very busy packed with locals, but very good food at a very non-tourist price. Good fuul and falafel. Large restaurant on 26th July St, just off Talaat Harb St, in downtown Cairo. They…"],["Koshari Achmat","restaurant",30.0582,31.24862,"","","","","","r","Decent and inexpensive Koshari."],["Fish & Chips","restaurant",30.04516,31.24267,"37 شارع البستان, Haret Al Hakr","","","","","r","The place is nostalgic of good old times. It's cozy and a bit quirky. Nice decorations. The crunchy bread slices are unique. It's a woman-run business. The shrimp stuffed fillet is delicious."],["La Chesa","restaurant",30.05126,31.24382,"21 Adly St.","","","","","r","Serving fondues, and other traditional Swiss dishes, pizza, salads and patisseries, this is one of the better continental restaurants in Downtown Cairo."],["Costa Coffee","restaurant",30.0489,31.24227,"26 Sherif Basha","","","","","r","Modern coffee chain that also serves desserts and some sandwiches"],["Tawfiqiyya Souq","bar",30.0536,31.2426,"","","","","","r","Lots of coffee shops and lots of atmosphere."],["El Horreya Cafe and Bar","bar",30.04529,31.24039,"","","","","","r","While noisy and crowded, this classic baladi bar (the Cairene take on a dive bar) is one of very few left in the city centre."]]}